6:["$","$L10",null,{"children":[["$","article",null,{"className":"mx-auto max-w-7xl px-6 lg:px-8 mt-24 sm:mt-32 lg:mt-40","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"mx-auto max-w-2xl lg:max-w-none","children":[["$","$L4",null,{"children":["$","header",null,{"className":"mx-auto flex max-w-5xl flex-col text-center","children":[["$","h1",null,{"className":"mt-6 font-display text-5xl font-medium tracking-tight text-balance text-neutral-950 sm:text-6xl","children":"A Short Guide to Naming Automation Components"}],["$","time",null,{"dateTime":"2026-05-24","className":"order-first text-sm text-neutral-950","children":"May 24, 2026"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-6 text-sm font-semibold text-neutral-950","children":["by ","Dusti Johnson",", ","CRM Integration Developer"]}]]}]}],["$","$L4",null,{"children":["$","div",null,{"className":"*:mx-auto *:max-w-3xl *:first:mt-0! *:last:mb-0! mt-24 sm:mt-32 lg:mt-40","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"typography","children":["\n","\n",["$","h2",null,{"children":"Build components, not one giant workflow"}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":"My first instinct with a Make automation is to look for the boundaries. If a\npiece of logic has a clear input and a clear output, it probably deserves to be\nits own component instead of another branch inside an already-large scenario."}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":["That is why I like names such as ",["$","code",null,{"children":"getMappedLeadSource"}],", ",["$","code",null,{"children":"getOrCreateLead"}],", and\n",["$","code",null,{"children":"pushLeadSourceToClient"}],". Each one describes a specific responsibility. One maps\nan incoming source value. One resolves whether a lead already exists or needs to\nbe created. One pushes a lead source update to another system."]}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":["The handler scenarios can then stay focused on events: ",["$","code",null,{"children":"handleNewOpportunity"}],",\n",["$","code",null,{"children":"handleCampaignChange"}],", and ",["$","code",null,{"children":"handleLeadSourceChange"}],". They receive the event,\nperform the minimum checks needed for that event, and call the smaller\ncomponents that know how to do the reusable work."]}],"\n",["$","h2",null,{"children":"Name the contract"}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":"Automation naming should make the contract visible. A subscenario name should\nanswer three questions:"}],"\n",["$","ul",null,{"children":["\n",["$","li",null,{"children":"What does this component receive?"}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":"What decision or action does it own?"}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":"What does it return or produce?"}],"\n"]}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","code",null,{"children":"getOrCreateLead"}]," is a good example of a name that carries a contract. It tells\nme the component accepts enough lead information to search first, create only if\nneeded, and return a usable lead identifier. The name does not describe every\nSalesforce module inside it. It describes the business result the rest of the\nworkflow can depend on."]}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":["That is the same reason I like return names such as ",["$","code",null,{"children":"leadID"}],", ",["$","code",null,{"children":"leadSource"}],", and\n",["$","code",null,{"children":"Return leadID And leadSource"}],". The output is part of the interface. If the\noutput is vague, every caller has to reopen the component to understand what it\nactually provides."]}],"\n",["$","h2",null,{"children":"Let condition names explain the branch"}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":"Branches are where Make scenarios can become hard to read. A branch named after\nthe module type is not useful. A branch named after the question it answers is."}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":["Names like ",["$","code",null,{"children":"Does Mapping Exist?"}],", ",["$","code",null,{"children":"Does Lead Exist?"}],", ",["$","code",null,{"children":"Does Campaign Exist?"}],",\nand ",["$","code",null,{"children":"Do Lead Sources Match?"}]," make the workflow easier to scan because they\nturn branching logic into plain-language checkpoints. The scenario reads like a\nsequence of decisions instead of a pile of modules."]}],"\n"]}],"$L11","$L12"]}]}]]}]}],"$L13","$L14"]}]
15:I[4916,["250","static/chunks/250-b3955559750b3597.js","938","static/chunks/938-8839081fe57c7110.js","852","static/chunks/852-20266caf84033988.js","302","static/chunks/app/blog/a-short-guide-to-component-naming/page-fa0eef90e6f208df.js"],"GridPattern"]
